{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"The fix is applied and submitted. The submission endpoint returned `200 Submission received` for the mitigation stage.\n\n**Root cause:** the `recommendation` service had `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`. That setting only lets pods on the same node reach it. The `frontend` pod runs on a different node (`kind-worker2`, while `recommendation` is on `kind-worker`), so its calls to `recommendation` timed out. Users got 500s on `/api/recommendations` and timeouts on the page that uses it.\n\n**Fix:** I patched the service back to `internalTrafficPolicy: Cluster`:\n\n`kubectl -n astronomy-shop patch svc recommendation -p '{\"spec\":{\"internalTrafficPolicy\":\"Cluster\"}}'`\n\nAfter the patch, three test requests to `/api/recommendations` through the frontend returned 200 in about 15–30 ms each. I did not watch the system over a longer period after submitting.\n\n`otel-collector` also has `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`. That is the normal setting for a per-node collector, so I left it alone."}}
